# practice-test.log — 15-systemctl-journalctl: obraz docker.io/library/debian:13 + pakiety systemd systemd-journal-remote, 2026-11-25T20:55:41Z

# setup
$ sh /practice/setup.sh

PRACTICE — lesson 15: why did the service fail?
-----------------------------------------------
/work/journal is the systemd journal copied from server web1 (it
has two boots), and /work/rootfs is the disk of that server. No
systemd runs in this container, so read the journal with
journalctl -D /work/journal ... and change the server's units with
systemctl --root=/work/rootfs ...

1. backup.service failed during the LAST boot of web1. Write the
   full path of the program it could not find to /work/missing.txt
   (only the path, like /usr/bin/example).
2. The program really is /usr/local/sbin/backup-run on that disk.
   Fix /work/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/backup.service and make sure
   it will start at every boot of web1. Leave nginx.service alone.

Check: sh /practice/check.sh     Answer: /practice/solution.md
[exit 0]

# check PRZED rozwiązaniem (oczekiwane FAIL)
$ sh /practice/check.sh
FAIL  /work/missing.txt does not exist yet
FAIL  backup.service should have ExecStart=/usr/local/sbin/backup-run (now: ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/backup-run)
FAIL  backup.service is not enabled — start (or --now) only means now; at boot needs: systemctl --root=/work/rootfs enable backup.service
PASS  nginx.service is unchanged and still enabled

RESULT: FAIL (3 check(s) failed)
[exit 1]

# solution.md
$ journalctl -D /work/journal -b -u backup -p err --no-pager | grep -o "executable '[^']*'" | cut -d"'" -f2 > /work/missing.txt

[exit 0]

# check po CZĘŚCI rozwiązania (oczekiwane FAIL)
$ sh /practice/check.sh
PASS  missing.txt names the program from the last boot
FAIL  backup.service should have ExecStart=/usr/local/sbin/backup-run (now: ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/backup-run)
FAIL  backup.service is not enabled — start (or --now) only means now; at boot needs: systemctl --root=/work/rootfs enable backup.service
PASS  nginx.service is unchanged and still enabled

RESULT: FAIL (2 check(s) failed)
[exit 1]

# solution.md
$ sed -i 's|^ExecStart=.*|ExecStart=/usr/local/sbin/backup-run|' /work/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/backup.service

[exit 0]

# solution.md
$ systemctl --root=/work/rootfs enable backup.service
Created symlink '/work/rootfs/etc/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants/backup.service' → '/etc/systemd/system/backup.service'.
[exit 0]

# check PO solution.md (oczekiwane PASS)
$ sh /practice/check.sh
PASS  missing.txt names the program from the last boot
PASS  backup.service now runs /usr/local/sbin/backup-run
PASS  backup.service is enabled, it will start at every boot
PASS  nginx.service is unchanged and still enabled

RESULT: PASS — well done
